course: dictionary
lesson: 8898
title: Shrubs: the bushes in between
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A shrub is a woody plant that is smaller than a tree. It has several stems growing from near the ground, so it looks bushy. Another word for a shrub is a bush.
explain: «Goats prefer leaves, twigs and shrubs to grass.» Goats like shrubs more than grass, so shrubs must be plants with leaves and twigs that goats can eat. The word sits in a list next to leaves and twigs, which is a clue that it is a kind of plant.
explain: «Under the canopy lies the understorey, a dim world of young trees, shrubs, vines and big-leaved plants.» Shrubs are listed with young trees and vines, so they grow in the forest below the tall trees, in the dim light.
fact: A shrub is a woody plant smaller than a tree, with several stems growing from near the ground.
fact: Lavender, rosemary, holly, hydrangea and gorse are all shrubs.
fact: Gardens and parks often have a shrub border, a row of shrubs along a path or fence.
fact: Birds can nest in shrubs.
fact: Shrubs sit between small plants and trees.
exercise: Which of these is a shrub? | Daisy | *Holly | Blade of grass | Oak tree
exercise: «Goats prefer leaves, twigs and shrubs to grass.» What does shrubs mean here? | Tall trees with fruit | Animals that live in the grass | *Woody plants smaller than trees | Stones on a path
exercise: Where might a bird build its nest? | In the clouds | Inside a glass bottle | Under the sea | *Inside a shrub
test: What is another name for a shrub? | *A bush | A stone | A tree | A flower
test: In the forest in the text, where do shrubs grow? | *Under the canopy, in the understorey | Above the canopy, in the open sky | In the river | On the top of the tallest tree
exam: Which of these is NOT a shrub? | Lavender | Hydrangea | Gorse | *Oak
